loader-rosetta-x87.patch - Gamify patch over CrossOver 25.1.0 Wine (dlls/ntdll/unix), LGPL-2.1-or-later.
Start i386 processes under the x87sidecar (https://github.com/athei/x87sidecar, MIT) in cooperative
mode when ROSETTA_X87_PATH names its binary, so that its x87 JIT hook replaces Rosetta's slow
software emulation of x87 (32-bit Unity/Mono games, NOTES 2026-11-06). Ported from athei/wine
branch cx-26-patched, commit f837e313f7 "ntdll: HACK: Start i386 processes under the x87sidecar
cooperatively", without its compatdb.so rules and without a bundled default (only the variable
turns it on, so the runtime is unchanged without it). Changes against that patch, because
CrossOver 25.1 on macOS has no preloader and runs an i386 program of the first process in the
same process (WoW64): an i386 child is re-exec'd as `x87sidecar --cooperative <loader> <args>`
from preloader_exec() (machine from exec_wineloader), and the first process of a launch (no
WINESERVERSOCKET) re-execs itself the same way when its first argument is an existing i386 PE
file (WINEX87SIDECARSTARTED stops a loop). __wine_main hands the task port to the sidecar
(x87_cooperative_handshake, verbatim from athei) and prints a "RUNNING WITHOUT X87 ACCELERATION"
banner when the hook could not be installed. coop_proto.h is a verbatim copy of x87sidecar's
rosetta_loader/src/coop_proto.h (the other end of the Mach handshake). Details: NOTES.md, docs/app.md "x87 acceleration".

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/coop_proto.h
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/coop_proto.h
